The attached image compares the anti-recombinant Protective Antigen (rPA) IgG antibody titers in mice immunized with rPA alone, or rPA combined with different doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 adjuvants. The data demonstrate that both Nano-11 and AH significantly enhance the antibody response compared to soluble rPA. Notably, Nano-11 at 50 µg/dose and 200 µg/dose induces antibody titers that are comparable to or even greater than those achieved with equivalent doses of AH, consistent with the findings in Section 3.5 that Nano-11 strongly enhances the antibody response to vaccine antigens.